      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Adaptation of https://github.com/axiomgraph/ComfyUIWorkflow/blob/main/Mage%20Flow%20Edit.json created by axiomgraph, with the sampler settings from https://github.com/starsFriday/ComfyUI-MageFlow and https://github.com/zhaotututu/ComfyUI-MageFlow.\n\n### No custom node needed\n\nComfyUI ships Mage-Flow support in core — `comfy/ldm/mage_flow`, the `mage` CLIP type and `TextEncodeMageFlowEdit` — so this runs on stock loaders. The community packs add convenience wrappers (an all-in-one loader) or a Diffusers-directory path that pulls in `diffusers` plus Microsoft's pinned source; neither buys anything core does not already do, so neither is installed.\n\n### Mage-Flow Edit\n\nThe RL-aligned edit model: 30 steps at CFG 5.0, euler / simple. Write an **instruction**, not a description of the finished image.\n\n`Reference image 2` is muted by default. Unmute it for a two-reference edit (\"put the jacket from image 2 on the person in image 1\") — the encoder takes up to 16 references and resizes them all to the output resolution, because Mage's RoPE aligns reference and target by position.\n\n`width` / `height` at 0 keep the first reference's own size, floored to a multiple of 16.\n\n### Model links\n\n```dotenv\nCOMFY_ASSET_PROFILES=mage-flow-edit\n```\n\nEverything comes from [Comfy-Org/Mage-Flow](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Mage-Flow), ungated, and the loaders carry `properties.models` — so the stack provisions itself through the example-workflow scan whether or not the profile is selected, the same way every other bundled template here behaves. Comment the module out of `COMFY_CUSTOM_NODE_EXAMPLE_WORKFLOWS_ALLOWLIST` if you want these 17 GB off a machine that will never edit an image.\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/models/\n├── 📂 diffusion_models/mage_flow_edit_bf16.safetensors\n├── 📂 text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors\n└── 📂 vae/mage_flow_vae_bf16.safetensors\n```\n\nAlready running a `krea-2-*` profile? Point the CLIP loader at the 4.9 GB `qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors` you already have instead of the 8.3 GB bf16 file — same Qwen3-VL-4B encoder, and the `mage` type applies the prompt template either way.\n\n### Why there is no NVFP4 build here\n\nThe `ajh-code/Mage-Flow-NVFP4-*` repos are standalone Diffusers pipelines shipping prebuilt `libmage_nvfp4_linear.so` CUDA kernels, not safetensors ComfyUI can load. The smallest ComfyUI-loadable builds are Comfy-Org's official `int8_convrot` quants at 3.9 GB. They are not provisioned: on a machine with this much memory they are a pure quality loss, and having both builds on disk is how you end up downloading Mage-Flow twice. If you want one, point the loader at `mage_flow_edit_int8_convrot.safetensors` and add it to `asset-profiles.json`.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Credit, models and settings",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
